{"title":"2024 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2024 AMC 10B #14</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2024 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">2024 AMC 12B #9</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy_⚡🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_Ani_lytical_(5_minutes!⚡)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by Ani_lytical (5 minutes!⚡)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A dartboard is the region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> in the coordinate plane consisting of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/f/adfd9ae8a3fac031d3b8b470a52a709a23d4d6d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0d611043f1be322d4e55b86ea69609ced3a796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + |y| \\le 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />. A target <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the region where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/9/d191d0afb6626b84fbee717db5a70935f6e81d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2 + y^2 - 25)^2 \\le 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" />. A dart is thrown and lands at a random point in B. The probability that the dart lands in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/a/81a57a55c6ae7038b60d65938db833c70e86c42c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n} \\cdot \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"33\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2efed509b347679121e79b8fe639744b385ec6fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }39 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }71 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }73 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }75 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }135 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"443\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/033f5ec7de3fd0710af486d82a9cfbd5cad11a1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // By Elephant200 // Feel free to adjust the code  size(10cm);  pair A = (8, 0); pair B = (0, 8); pair C = (-8, 0); pair D = (0, -8); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(1.5));  label(&quot;$(8,0)$&quot;, A, NE); label(&quot;$(0,8)$&quot;, B, NE); label(&quot;$(-8,0)$&quot;, C, NW); label(&quot;$(0,-8)$&quot;, D, SE);  filldraw(circle((0,0),4*sqrt(2)), gray, linewidth(1.5)); filldraw(circle((0,0),3*sqrt(2)), white, linewidth(1.5));  draw((-10, 0)--(10,0),EndArrow(5)); draw((10, 0)--(-10,0),EndArrow(5)); draw((0,-10)--(0,10), EndArrow(5)); draw((0,10)--(0,-10),EndArrow(5)); [/asy]\" width=\"475\" height=\"448\" />\n~Elephant200\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Inequalities of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec8e900386db73d1605bf3ed8783e97ec0ff116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x|+|y| \\le 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> are well-known and correspond to a square in space with centre at origin and vertices at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/9/2e9ef6a89406ed156700a9899b3dd53973f10bf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(8, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/985856518244747eb2e1431581a512e3c06c9631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-8, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/6/b0626999ec3a98f3d1c031fea7cccc5b00d999ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85adc9ad9cea412a9fe9318b074859eda8ab5775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, -8)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />.\nThe diagonal length of this square is clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so it has an area of \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a66fdc982311cb313225cf592a68b0cc98e45f3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 16 \\cdot 16 = 128\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />\nNow,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/5/0a51bc9364a32d91a5f2fc59c5d48fd738cfd599.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^2 + y^2 - 25)^2 \\le 49\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"20\" />\nConverting to polar form,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/7/6974d2bba1243fb5f765acd6432a696a68b3aa93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2 - 25 \\le 7 \\implies r \\le \\sqrt{32},\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/8/4f861463709428b4887973a736f196b5ed62c65e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r^2 - 25 \\ge -7\\implies r\\ge \\sqrt{18}.\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>The intersection of these inequalities is the circular region <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> for which every circle in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has a radius between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/9/989baee15d26f4658aeda53a2e5015e3a205d182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d0aa7b903e0abe865f49e1a18c19f41dd8862a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{32}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, inclusive. The area of such a region is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/25909cbd81355196d2b4864e8d5c4621fe300472.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi(32-18)=14\\pi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" /> The requested probability is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/a/1ca08e67acc6aecc1ca73915523c14c2845e665e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{14\\pi}{128} = \\frac{7\\pi}{64},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" /> yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cdbed780eeb8cdf7c7ccd60293c0edbf7201951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m,n)=(7,64).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" /> We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/a/dca3b8118486f51a5d775b4e7f823e28bb533c24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n=7+64=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 71}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"217\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>-AbhiSood1234, countmath1\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Calculus)\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expressing the Area of Region \\( B \\)\n</p><p>Region \\( B \\) consists of points where \\( |x| + |y| \\le 8 \\)\n</p><p>In each quadrant, this can be expressed by the following functions:\n</p><p>First quadrant: \\( y = 8 - x \\)\nSecond quadrant: \\( y = 8 + x \\)\nThird quadrant: \\( y = -8 - x \\)\nFourth quadrant: \\( y = -8 + x \\)\n</p><p>In the first quadrant, \\( x \\) ranges from 0 to 8, and \\( y \\) ranges from 0 to \\( 8 - x \\). Thus, the area in the first quadrant is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ecbfd14603f6f359bd9e3d9eefacc463f69deb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area of first quadrant} = \\int_0^8 \\int_0^{8 - x} \\, dy \\, dx\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d1258f21c9ad5271f3c7ccb8e44e6fd31cdaaeb2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\int_0^8 [y]_{y=0}^{y=8-x} \\, dx = \\int_0^8 (8 - x) \\, dx\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408937ea6388cc5dddda73b8ac4efe0b8947a216.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\left[ 8x - \\frac{x^2}{2} \\right]_0^8 = 64 - 32 = 32\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"48\" />\nThe total area of region \\( B \\) is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00a942430e9f263e291d30aa3af48747d3cdcdd3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area of } B = 4 \\times 32 = 128\\]\" width=\"197\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Expressing the Area of Region \\( T \\)\nRegion \\( T \\) is defined by the inequality \\( (x^2 + y^2 - 25)^2 \\le 49 \\), which can be rewritten as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/042f941111df9981eb98f4861124d374c8c09d02.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[18 \\le x^2 + y^2 \\le 32\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>To find the area, we switch to polar coordinates with \\( x = r \\cos \\theta \\) and \\( y = r \\sin \\theta \\), where \\( x^2 + y^2 = r^2 \\). Here, \\( r \\) ranges from \\( \\sqrt{18} \\) to \\( \\sqrt{32} \\), and \\( \\theta \\) ranges from 0 to \\( 2\\pi \\).\n</p><p>The area of \\( T \\) can then be found by:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92d2547c7197ac01e4d1c620fb687e1e5f3742d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\text{Area of } T = \\int_0^{2\\pi} \\int_{\\sqrt{18}}^{\\sqrt{32}} r \\, dr \\, d\\theta\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"48\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e70fea1b687b29957e9595e4b1fc6a479f80f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\int_0^{2\\pi} \\left[ \\frac{r^2}{2} \\right]_{r=\\sqrt{18}}^{r=\\sqrt{32}} \\, d\\theta = \\int_0^{2\\pi} \\left( \\frac{32}{2} - \\frac{18}{2} \\right) \\, d\\theta\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"52\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73269498478cd537a703f9e3ec240fef869c00e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\int_0^{2\\pi} 7 \\, d\\theta = 14\\pi\\]\" width=\"138\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>The probability \\( P \\) that a dart lands in region \\( T \\) is the area of \\( T \\) divided by the area of \\( B \\):\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c721397c0d2d0abf3681e5124570e8560545f52c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P = \\frac{\\text{Area of } T}{\\text{Area of } B} = \\frac{14\\pi}{128} = \\frac{7\\pi}{64}\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>So the probability is of the form \\( \\frac{m}{n} \\pi \\), where \\( m = 7 \\) and \\( n = 64 \\), so \\( m + n = 7 + 64 = 71 \\).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c5b8e7e702c77154d158c23b27bc309782decc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 71}\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Athmyx\">Athmyx</a>\n</p><p>By the way never pull out calculus on the amc10. Itis time consuming and easy to make mistakes on\n~[minor edits by hao11]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_AMC_12B_P09.jpeg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cd/2024_AMC_12B_P09.jpeg/600px-2024_AMC_12B_P09.jpeg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"600\" height=\"849\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/c/cd/2024_AMC_12B_P09.jpeg/900px-2024_AMC_12B_P09.jpeg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/c/cd/2024_AMC_12B_P09.jpeg 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>~Kathan\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy_.E2.9A.A1.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy_⚡🚀)\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YqKmvSR1Ckk?feature=shared\">https://youtu.be/YqKmvSR1Ckk?feature=shared</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Zk9eW4lpTjo?si=qGMDoWy9WiNNG3yx\">https://youtu.be/Zk9eW4lpTjo?si=qGMDoWy9WiNNG3yx</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution 3 by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>